.TH "SCREENSHOT-LOCATION_MAC.SH" "1" "November 2026" "arran4/dotfiles" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
screenshot\-location_mac.sh \- configure a macOS screenshot destination
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBscreenshot\-location_mac.sh\fR
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create a Screenshots/mac screenshots directory in the home directory and set the com.apple.screencapture location preference to it using defaults.
.SH NOTES
This macOS\-only helper uses mkdir without \-p: it can fail if the directory already exists or its parent is absent.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Requires macOS and defaults. The script invokes mkdir without -p,
so ~/Screenshots must exist and the target directory must not
already exist.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
mkdir -p "$HOME/Screenshots"
screenshot-location_mac.sh
defaults read com.apple.screencapture location
.fi
.SH OPERATION AND CAVEATS
Creates the directory "mac screenshots" and writes its full
path to the com.apple.screencapture location preference.
A second invocation may fail because the directory exists.
Existing screenshots are not moved or deleted.
